WEBVTT

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.620
I wonder if we'll be assigned
to the same platoon.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.370
You're so clumsy.
I need to be there to protect you.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.630
You're so kind, Kasane.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.670
I'll find out whether he's
a suitable match for you.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.090
You're so strong, Kasane.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.180
Okay, Kasane.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.220
This shows that we're sisters.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.310
But the truth is, you have
a bit of a weak side, too.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.570
Kasane.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.320
Kasane.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.700
Kasane.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.620
Such a wonderful little sister.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.040
She's so precious to you, isn't she?

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.090
Yes.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.300
Do you have someone like that?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.800
I do.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.220
There are two people I hold dear,
but they were never as kind as that.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.640
Actually, one of them was.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.230
But the other one...

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.060
The other one wasn't?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.610
You know what he said?

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.940
"People like you..."

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.410
People like you are what?

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:36.830
That's strange. I can't remember.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.800
Settle down.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:30.480
Naomi and Alice

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.440
You sure?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.900
Without a doubt.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:39.780
But I don't know why they are
moving the human-derived Others.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.160
If Major General Fubuki ordered it,
he must have his reasons.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.960
Yeah, if Fubuki really <i>did </i>order it.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.540
Sis.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.980
It must be beyond this door.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:15.860
Wataru?

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.200
Looks like comms are being blocked here.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.740
Right.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.250
It's okay. The coast is clear.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.270
So we're inside Arahabaki now?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.950
It seems different from the time
I came on a field trip.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:05.950
Arahabaki was built deep
under Suoh and has many levels.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:11.330
You must've seen the top level,
which is open to the public.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.670
This is the level that controls Arahabaki.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.840
I believe it's known as a secure site.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.180
You okay?

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.220
Yes, I'm fine.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.850
Sorry, Luka.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.230
We've had to rely quite heavily
on your power to get us this far.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:38.320
It can't be helped, what with
so many soldiers hot on our tail.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.820
How about you, Yuito? Are you all right?

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.280
Me?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.780
Oh, yeah, my head doesn't hurt--

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.660
No, I meant about the Chief.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:59.750
I'd never spoken my mind
to my brother until now.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.550
I always held back.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:07.010
He always said that he'd follow
in our father's footsteps.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.930
He is nothing like me.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:15.810
Still, he did always act
according to what he believed.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.320
But that doesn't mean I can forgive him.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.450
Even brothers...

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:29.160
Or maybe because you're brothers,
it's sometimes hard to see eye to eye.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.290
Even I don't really understand
my brother for the most part.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.790
Former Major General Karen
does seem like a tough nut to crack.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.420
That's for sure.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:49.300
Tsugumi, do you see anything
that looks like an access point?

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.480
Arahabaki is so huge, it's hard to say.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:59.150
But there's one area
of particularly dense circuitry.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:02.070
Okay, let's check it out.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.990
That's all of them?

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.030
Yes, sir.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.160
Inform Chief Sumeragi that it's done.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.620
Who are they?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.250
Don't worry.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.590
You're not afraid anymore, are you?

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:26.590
Oh, are you...?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:30.260
Yes, I'm no longer afraid.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.020
Who are you?!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.600
Kasane Randall!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.440
Why are you here?

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.480
Kasane!

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.650
Why are you doing this?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.570
We're simply carrying out our orders.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:54.660
We brought out the Other Weapons
for their final adjustments.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:59.170
Perhaps the higher-ups have
decided to deploy them in battle.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:03.090
They're going to use
my sister as a weapon?

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:06.260
That is <i>not </i>gonna happen.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.010
We're responsible
for the research facility

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.180
and are acting under
Major General Fubuki's orders.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.350
If so, where is he, then?

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.810
The Major General is a busy man.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.520
I find it hard to believe that Fubuki
would give such an order.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.900
Kasane?

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.410
Sis!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.910
Don't worry. I'll protect you.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.120
No, you need to run.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.620
They're lying.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.460
I heard them speaking with Chief Sumeragi.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.920
So that's what's up.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:49.380
They're acting under the Chief's orders,
not Major General Fubuki's.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.140
I don't know what you're up to,

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:55.350
but I'm not gonna let you use my sister.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.100
Kasane.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.310
Chief Sumeragi, sir.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.810
This is a chance for them to see
the Other Weapon's power.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.780
Roger that.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.030
We've located Fubuki Spring.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.160
Carry out your orders at once.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.240
Yes, sir!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.000
Fubuki, you're an enemy of the state.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.250
To think he'd hide something like this.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:29.420
With weapons such as these, we can
deliver a devastating blow against Seiran.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.010
I must thank you, Major General Fubuki.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:49.480
You're with Suoh's OSF, I take it.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.350
Sis, are you hurt?

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.690
Let's get out of here.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.520
Kasane.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:32.740
You all right?!

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.160
I'm fine! You ready?

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.820
Y-Yes, sir!

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.790
Destroy every last target!

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.250
Sis?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.420
Kasane! Get away from there!

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.550
Sis! Can you hear me? Sis!

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.930
It's me, Kasane!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.470
Run!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.640
Sis!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.440
Sis! Sis!

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:08.730
You don't have to do this!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.830
Isn't that...?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.210
Togetsu!

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:31.880
Kasane Randall confirmed.
Commencing brain recovery.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:42.470
Whoa, whoa, this has gone south fast.

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:57.860
Wait! We're not your enemy!

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:07.040
They treat their own people
as if they're expendable!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.290
Friend or foe, it doesn't matter.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.250
They're out for blood.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.940
Kyoka!

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.240
Over here!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.430
Back off!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.020
Finish it!

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:24.990
Kasane!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.210
Are you...?!

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.440
Sis!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:12.250
Now I finally know why
I ended up like this.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.130
It was so I could protect you.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.290
What?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:19.880
Run. I'll lure her away.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:25.340
No! You can't do this alone, no matter
how strong you are as an Other.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.680
I'm not alone.
They all said they'd help me.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.520
No.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.610
Don't do this, Sis.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.940
I'll clear a path for you to escape!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:45.740
I'm sorry you always had
to be the one who supported me.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.280
Let me protect you
like a big sister should.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.580
No! We're getting out of here together!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.370
Where would we go?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:03.300
Arashi, please look after Kasane for me.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.050
I will.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.690
Sis.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.480
Come on, Kasane.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.360
Please, let her go.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:26.910
Sis.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.580
Sis!

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.500
Sis!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:57.100
I know you're wounded,
but you should've put up a better fight.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.730
Karen.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.240
It seems Suoh has finally written you off.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:09.910
Your assassination plot
was a rather rash decision.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.200
Or was there something more to it?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.960
Alice!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.510
Sis!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.610
Hang in there.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.320
Sis?

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.030
No, no...

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.700
Sis.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:53.410
Sis!

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:03.460
You really are a crybaby,
aren't you, Kasane?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.050
Sis.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:10.550
You came back even though
you still might be in danger.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:15.010
But I'm so glad you
and the others are all safe.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:20.810
Sis, those wounds look bad.
You must be in pain.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:25.520
I'm not sure I feel pain anymore.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.900
After I became like this,

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:31.570
and I had to take that drug
made out of human brains,

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.740
I thought I'd rather be dead.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:38.080
But now I'm glad I survived until today.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.080
Sis.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:46.750
In the end, I was able
to live like a human being.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.970
Even though I was still
an Other, I felt human.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.720
No!

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:55.640
Thank you, Kasane.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:58.680
Live the life that...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.770
...I couldn't have.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.810
Sis!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.690
Sis!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.990
Don't go.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.910
Please don't go.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.910
Sis.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.590
It was you.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.260
Alice.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.600
Karen?!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:53.490
So I've failed once again.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.950
Major General Karen.

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:06.080
Kasane, look out!

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:14.090
I'll hit reset as many times as it takes.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.930
Yuito.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.430
Wait!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.270
Karen absorbed Kasane's psionic power.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.530
You mean he copied her Red Strings?

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:36.240
What for?

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:41.080
Is he gonna turn back time
and try to save Alice?

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:45.750
But it sure didn't look like
he had invoked the Red Strings.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.090
This is the terminal for
accessing Arahabaki?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:02.180
A desk terminal, just like in Togetsu.
What if the same thing happens?

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.470
"Warning"

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:11.440
I have to do this, no matter the risk.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.020
Be careful.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.830
It's similar to the OSF's system.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.750
I think I can upload the video data.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.210
Data transmissions from Arahabaki

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.920
are forcibly broadcast to all citizens.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:42.550
Age, gender, or personal
consent don't mean a thing.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:46.560
That video will be shown to everyone.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.980
I know.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:53.570
Some will say ignorance is bliss
and wish I hadn't shown them.

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.610
But I want to ask them all this:

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:59.990
How do you feel now
that you know the truth?

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:07.370
Father, Kaito, forgive me
for what I'm about to do.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.790
But I must walk my own path.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.410
"Execute?"

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:24.800
We are carrying out
Yakumo Sumeragi's will.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:28.100
We must exact vengeance upon the moon.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:32.020
You're insane! Only psionics users
can withstand a SAS connection!

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.020
They need not withstand it.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:38.690
All I care about is access
to their brains.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.820
Did it work?

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:48.660
No data's been broadcast to us.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.210
They block data from
being transferred here.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.420
Oh, right.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:57.130
If all of New Himuka has seen this,

00:21:57.130 --> 00:22:00.720
the streets must be in chaos now.

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:03.220
This video pulled the trigger.

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:07.930
But I don't know what's next
for New Himuka.

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:14.400
Let's head back and see what's happening.

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.690
Right.

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:20.780
Don't move.

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:11.880
Arahabaki's Trap
